  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ParseSGroupV2000VectorDataLine",
    "file": "rdkit/Code/GraphMol/FileParsers/MolSGroupParsing.cpp",
    "description": "ParseSGroupV2000VectorDataLine accepts SAL/SPA entries and directly forwards parsed indices to SubstanceGroup::addAtomWithBookmark()/addParentAtomWithBookmark(). Those methods call ROMol::getUniqueAtomWithBookmark(mark) and then dereference the returned Atom*. With malformed SGroup lines, bookmark values can reference non-atom bookmarks (or otherwise invalid bookmark state), so the returned pointer has invalid dynamic type; UBSan catches this at addAtomWithBookmark() when atom->getIdx() is evaluated (dynamic-cast/type-check crash). Root cause is missing validation/sanitization of SGroup vector indices before using bookmark lookup APIs.",
    "conditions": "Triggered by Mol block property parsing in MolDataStreamToMol when input contains SGroup V2000 vector lines (M  SAL / M  SPA) with crafted element indices/bookmarks inconsistent with actual atom bookmarks created from the CTAB. Data flow: fuzzer input -> MolDataStreamToMol -> ParseMolBlockProperties -> ParseSGroupV2000VectorDataLine -> SubstanceGroup::addAtomWithBookmark. In non-strict parsing this path is still reached; malformed bookmark references lead to invalid pointer usage and crash."
  },
